==================================================
66. ARCHITECTURAL INVARIANTS
==================================================

The following rules are canonical:

1. Every important entity has an owner.

2. Every persistent entity has a lifecycle.

3. Temporary data is not automatically persistent.

4. Processing does not imply retention.

5. Storage location does not define ownership.

6. Derived data must remain traceable to its source where required.

7. Primary state is authoritative.

8. Derived state must be rebuildable whenever practical.

9. Security-critical data requires strong consistency.

10. Sensitive data must follow explicit privacy rules.

11. Deletion must account for dependent derived data.

12. Provider storage does not automatically transfer ownership.

13. Audit records must not become an unrestricted copy of user activity.

14. No subsystem may treat another subsystem's internal data as its own.

15. Human authority remains central to personal data.

