68. FINAL CANONICAL PRINCIPLE
==================================================

PRSL-AI does not treat all data equally.

Data has:

Meaning.

Ownership.

Authority.

Sensitivity.

Lifecycle.

Persistence.

Provenance.

Consistency.

The architecture must know the difference between:

"What is happening now."

"What should be remembered."

"What is known."

"What was executed."

"What was verified."

"What is authorized."

"What belongs to the user."

"What belongs to the system."

"What came from an external source."

This separation is fundamental to maintaining privacy, reliability, modularity and architectural integrity.

